MF= 1 General information                                         9222 1451
  MT=452 Number of Neutrons per fission                           9222 1451
    Sum of MT=455 and 456.                                        9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
  MT=455 Delayed neutron data                                     9222 1451
    At the thermal neutron energy, nu-d of 0.0067 was obtained    9222 1451
    from the data of Borzakov et al./2/, Conant et al./3/ and     9222 1451
    Keepin et al./4/.                                             9222 1451
    Nu-d above 10 keV was determined from experimental data       9222 1451
    measured by Krick and Evans/5,6/, Piksaykin et al./7/,        9222 1451
    and Masters et al./8/.                                        9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
    Decay constants were taken from Ref./9/.                      9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
  MT=456 Number of prompt neutrons per fission                    9222 1451
    Nu-p was determined from the data of Protopopov et al./10/,   9222 1451
    Smirenkin et al./11/, Flerov et al./12/, Hopkins et al./13/,  9222 1451
    Colvin et al./14,15/, Mather et al./16/, Walsh et al./17/,    9222 1451
    Hockenbury/18/, Nurpeisov et al./19,20/, Sergachev et al./21/,9222 1451
    Nefedov et al./22/, and Gwin et al./23,24/                    9222 1451
    Nu-p of Cf-252 SF = 3.756+-0.031 /25/ was used.               9222 1451
    They were reproduced with two straight lines below and above  9222 1451
    about 1.5 MeV.                                                9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
  MT=458 Components of energy release due to fission              9222 1451
    Total energy and prompt energy were calculated from mass      9222 1451
    balance using JENDL-4 fission yields data and mass excess     9222 1451
    evaluation. Mass excess values were from Audi's 2009          9222 1451
    evaluation/26/. Delayed energy values were calculated from    9222 1451
    the energy release for infinite irradiation using JENDL FP    9222 1451
    Decay Data File 2000 and JENDL-4 yields data. For delayed     9222 1451
    neutron energy, as the JENDL FP Decay Data File 2000/27/ does 9222 1451
    not include average neutron energy values, the average values 9222 1451
    were calculated using the formula shown in the report by      9222 1451
    T.R. England/28/. The fractions of prompt energy were         9222 1451
    calculated using the fractions of Sher's evaluation/29/ when  9222 1451
    they were provided. When the fractions were not given by Sher,9222 1451
    averaged fractions were used.                                 9222 1451
