MF= 3 Neutron cross sections                                      9222 1451
  Cross sections above the resolved resonance region except for   9222 1451
  the total (MT=1), elastic scattering (MT=2) and fission cross   9222 1451
  sections (MT=18, 19, 20, 21, 38) were calculated with CCONE     9222 1451
  code/31/. The model parameters were determined by considering   9222 1451
  integral experimental data as well as measured cross-section    9222 1451
  data.                                                           9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
  In the CCONE calculation the CC OMP of Soukhovitskii et al./32/ 9222 1451
  was modified so as to reproduce well the experimental data of   9222 1451
  total cross section measured by Poenitz et al./33,34/ and       9222 1451
  Guber et al./35/                                                9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
  Other parameters of CCONE calculation were adjusted to the      9222 1451
  fission cross section of JENDL-3.3 and the capture cross section9222 1451
  measured by Hopkins and Diven/36/.                              9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
  The results of CC calculation for the elastic scattering was    9222 1451
  increased by 0.2 b above 1.5 MeV to improve integral benchmark  9222 1451
  tests.                                                          9222 1451
