    * Distributions were calculated with the modified Madland-Nix 9222 1451
      model/78,79/.  The compound nucleus formation cross         9222 1451
      sections for fission fragments (FF) were calculated using   9222 1451
      Becchetti-Greenlees potential/80/. Up to 4th-chance-fission 9222 1451
      were considered at high incident neuttron energies.         9222 1451
      The Ignatyuk formula/81/ were used to generate the level    9222 1451
      density parameters.                                         9222 1451
        Parameters adopted:                                       9222 1451
           Total average FF kinetic energy = 172.311-0.0212*E(MeV)9222 1451
           Average energy release          = 188.438 MeV          9222 1451
           Average mass number of light FF =  95                  9222 1451
           Average mass number of heavy FF = 139                  9222 1451
           Level density of the light FF   =  9.999- 10.094       9222 1451
           Level density of the heavy FF   = 11.89 - 12.20        9222 1451
        Note that the parameters vary with the incident energy    9222 1451
        within the indicated range.                               9222 1451
