Appendix A1: Resolved resonance parameters (ENDF/B-VII.0)         9222 1451
=========================================================         9222 1451
MT=151 RESOLVED AND UNRESOLVED RESONANCE PARAMETER EVALUATIONS    9222 1451
      L. Leal, H. Derrien, Guber, N. Larson, R. Wright,           9222 1451
               and R.Spencer (ORNL)                               9222 1451
                    January, 2003                                 9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
   The resonance parameter evaluation was done by Leal,           9222 1451
Derrien, Guber, Larson, Wright and Spencer [LE01] using the       9222 1451
multilevel R-matrix analysis code SAMMY [LA96].  The resolved     9222 1451
resonance evaluation were performed in the energy range from 0 to 9222 1451
600 eV. The unresolved resonance region evaluation covers the     9222 1451
energy range from 600 eV to 40 keV.                               9222 1451
   The evaluation included high resolution transmission data      9222 1451
(GU00), fission cross section data [GU98] measured at the Oak     9222 1451
Ridge Electron Linear Accelerator (ORELA), in addition to other   9222 1451
experimental data.  Integral data were also included in the       9222 1451
evaluation. Integral quantities and thermal values calculated     9222 1451
with the U-233 resonance parameter are shown in the Table below.  9222 1451
Also shown are the results of calculations using U-233 ENDF/B-VI  9222 1451
evaluation and Axton standard values:                             9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
                                                                  9222 1451
